# Changelog

- Read `CHANGELOG.md` before changing platform behavior.
- Update the active unreleased version in the same task as a user-visible
  feature or bug fix. Follow **How to write an entry** in `CHANGELOG.md`.
- Record only what a reader, member, or administrator can newly do (**Added**)
  or what stopped going wrong for them (**Fixed**). Group related changes.
  Skip empty sections, commit dumps, and duplicate bullets.
- Leave out services, migrations, configuration, deployment, tests, refactors,
  and API paths.
- The already-pushed baseline is 1.0.0 at commit
  `d9f05890c8d99e910b70880aeb9ad7df526b728d`. Current work belongs to 1.0.1 until
  it is released. Follow **How to write an entry** for subsequent versions.
- Never invent release dates, tags, or successful test results. Preserve
  released entries.
- Changelog-only edits do not need their own changelog entry.
